{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/835406-and-their-number-was-444-possible-setting-hack","id":835406,"title":"And Their Number Was 444 (possible setting hack)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-22T14:57:02-08:00","id":835406,"title":"And Their Number Was 444 (possible setting hack)","content":"just a random thought I've had.<br /> <br /> Demon's setting works under the assumption that each angel is for &quot;one time use&quot; most of the times. The God Machine creates each angel for a specific goal, and then recycles it when it finish the job. Sometimes, angels Fall, which is a bug in the system and a waste of resources- but theoretically, the God Machine can and would make a new angel in its place.<br /> <br /> Now, the question is- how different the setting would be if there was a limited number of angels in the whole world? I mean, what if once, long time ago, the God Machine created a Legion of angels- and it can't create anymore? Those angels have definite functions and are meant to serve certain goals, each time a different task. They know each other- or, at least, recognize each other. They have been around since the dawn of times- and every one an angel Falls, it can not be fixed- unless it is returned to the God Machine and &quot;re-programmed&quot;. Destroying an angel or a demon would be a huge harm to the God Machine, which would either need a long process to rebuild it, make a new angel in its place or even may not replace it in any possible way- what's fall would stay fallen (depends of how harsh we want it to be for that crazy engine of creation).<br /> <br /> In sort- how do you think such approach would change the setting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T15:08:48-08:00","id":835412,"title":"","content":"Well, the G-M looks a lot less imposing; it gives the setting a bit more of the feel of Fallen from WoD; everyone knows each other somewhat and they all have similiar experiences and social touchstones. Quite a neat idea.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T15:41:20-08:00","id":835430,"title":"","content":"I heard multiple users saying that the G-M can only account for mortals and Demons in Its plans, but I don't know where this is stated or implied. Under this setting hack, the G-M would logically decide to complement Its list of agents with supernatural pawns that aren't Demons, lest It lose crucial information for Its countless ongoing plans. If not that, a lot more Stigmatics, Demon-Blooded and Cryptids.<br /> <br /> A few hundred Angels sounds like far too little, even for a smaller G-M. I would raise that number to a few thousand. I know the title is a play on the Number Of The Beast, it's just a nitpick. It's likely that the Angels' average power level would increase in order to keep up with all that multi-tasking. Perhaps they would almost always have Rank 3+, with more Incepts.<br /> <br /> I like this idea. It raises the stakes, and allows for a less pervasive G-M should the group prefer that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 02-22-2016, 07:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T16:07:14-08:00","id":835438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/835406-and-their-number-was-444-possible-setting-hack?p=835430#post835430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I heard multiple users saying that the G-M can only account for mortals and Demons in Its plans, but I don't where this is stated or implied.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other supernaturals are beholden to more distant laws whose guiding intelligences are just as jealous and contradictory as the Machine. God has Its handholds in humanity and a small subset of monsters, but interference builds quickly when one supermassive black box tries to incorporate another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T16:11:06-08:00","id":835439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/835406-and-their-number-was-444-possible-setting-hack?p=835430#post835430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I heard multiple users saying that the G-M can only account for mortals and Demons in Its plans, but I don't where this is stated or implied. Under this setting hack, the G-M would logically decide to complement Its list of agents with supernatural pawns that aren't Demons, lest It lose crucial information for Its countless ongoing plans. If not that, a lot more Stigmatics, Demon-Blooded and Cryptids.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, to add what Satchel passed over, this idea was introduced in the original God-Machine Chronicle as one choice in the various list of answers to the question of &quot;What is the God-Machine/What does it want/Why is your character involved?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T16:33:00-08:00","id":835454,"title":"","content":"Surely it would be 4444?<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> I was going to go with <sup>4</sup>4 (4 to the 4th hyper-operation), but that would be larger than the number of particles in the universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 02-23-2016, 03:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T04:10:27-08:00","id":835670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/835406-and-their-number-was-444-possible-setting-hack?p=835454#post835454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Surely it would be 4444?<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> I was going to go with <sup>4</sup>4 (4 to the 4th hyper-operation), but that would be larger than the number of particles in the universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the God-Machine <i>does</i> manage multiple timelines...<br /> <br /> It would make company parties a bit crowded, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T06:29:33-08:00","id":835709,"title":"","content":"Well I already play it as such that angels are infinitely malleable- they can be rendered back into Essence and rebuilt any number of times. Now I don't do the whole &quot; finite number of angels&quot; thing, being a glitchy machine that it is, the G-M still has the power of a deity.. Summoning/building angels shouldn't be beyond its power at all methinks. That being said, my God-Machine very rarely builds angels due to the fact they are so configurable- no need to build new ones when one can just reformat an existing unit. But when it DOES build a new angel... That is a time for demons to be shitting their quantum existential pants... Or plotting its Fall before it can truly serve the Machine.<br /> <br /> Now as for a number of angels, I typically say that those currently in existence and not Fallen are somewhere in the neighborhood of one hundred thousand, with the number of active demons being close to around twenty thousand. Then again my scale is a little too conservative, but this is just my setting lol.<br /> <br /> For what you have though, it is very interesting and works well, if not showcasing a somewhat underpowered/super heavily damaged God-Machine. I quite like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 02-23-2016, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T07:29:02-08:00","id":835758,"title":"","content":"another random thought.<br /> <br /> Considering that if the number of angels is finite, then captured demons are not &quot;recycled&quot; as much as &quot;fixed&quot;- which could mean that, for some demons, it may not even be the first time they Fall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T09:22:52-08:00","id":835828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/835406-and-their-number-was-444-possible-setting-hack?p=835758#post835758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">another random thought.<br /> <br /> Considering that if the number of angels is finite, then captured demons are not &quot;recycled&quot; as much as &quot;fixed&quot;- which could mean that, for some demons, it may not even be the first time they Fall.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always assumed recycling was essentially that to be honest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T09:50:15-08:00","id":841355,"title":"","content":"If you're looking for imposing antagonists to play servant to the G-M in a &quot;finite angels&quot; setting, you could use Mages. In my particular version/interpretation of the WoD, the Seers of the Throne are unwittingly a G-M cult. The entities they believe to be the Exarchs are actually Rank 10 angels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2573-inkpenavenger","name":"inkpenavenger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2573_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T14:30:24-08:00","id":846274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>inkpenavenger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/835406-and-their-number-was-444-possible-setting-hack?p=841355#post841355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're looking for imposing antagonists to play servant to the G-M in a &quot;finite angels&quot; setting, you could use Mages. In my particular version/interpretation of the WoD, the Seers of the Throne are unwittingly a G-M cult. The entities they believe to be the Exarchs are actually Rank 10 angels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good god. Angels which can legitimately claim the power of the Unmoved Mover. Scary.<br /> <br /> Now that I've got that over with, I like the idea but I'd make them Rank 9, just for the sake of may sanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T15:06:07-08:00","id":846290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>inkpenavenger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/835406-and-their-number-was-444-possible-setting-hack?p=841355#post841355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're looking for imposing antagonists to play servant to the G-M in a &quot;finite angels&quot; setting, you could use Mages. In my particular version/interpretation of the WoD, the Seers of the Throne are unwittingly a G-M cult. The entities they believe to be the Exarchs are actually Rank 10 angels.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are the oracles then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T07:53:07-07:00","id":846566,"title":"","content":"Prolly the kings of Atlantis, trying to free their people from the God-Machine's control. Or they could be demons, whichever works","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T12:55:43-07:00","id":846685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/835406-and-their-number-was-444-possible-setting-hack?p=846566#post846566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prolly the kings of Atlantis, trying to free their people from the God-Machine's control. Or they could be demons, whichever works</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... Buncha Saboteurs only a step away from getting to their hells? Seems legit.<br /> Also eplains the ridiculous numbers of the Exarchs some Seers claim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T10:39:54-07:00","id":847186,"title":"","content":"If we are equating the Oracles to Saboteurs, then they have already reached their Hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T12:02:09-07:00","id":847229,"title":"","content":"TBH not quite, beacause they're still stuck in there with the most potent of GM's minions in an eternal struggle...<br /> What if they are Exarch Angels who became Unchained while in Supernal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T11:18:47-07:00","id":848289,"title":"","content":"Well the Storyteller's guide shows that one demon's Hell could be a plot by the God-Machineto capture other rogues, so make of that how you will. And hard to say","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}